INT. ABANDONED PLANETARIUM, LOBBY - NIGHT

A dead ticket booth. A mural of the solar system, flaking. On the counter, an old answering machine with its red light blinking.

The machine clicks. A tape whirs.

NKECHI (V.O.)
(recorded, level)
If you are hearing this, the dome is unlocked. Come alone. Do not touch the projector.

The tape ends. Silence. A fluorescent tube ticks. Then the heavy front door scrapes open.

INSPECTOR NKECHI ADEYEMI, 40s, crosses the threshold in a dark raincoat, flashlight held low, badge clipped to her belt. Short hair. A face that wastes no expression.

She stops at the counter. Looks at the machine. Presses play.

NKECHI (V.O.)
(recorded, level)
If you are hearing this, the dome is unlocked. Come alone. Do not touch the projector.

She presses stop, pockets the tape, and trains her flashlight on the doors of the dome.

NKECHI
(to herself)
I never left this message.

She pushes open the dome door. The beam falls across rows of empty seats.
